**
!Dockerfile
!pyproject.toml
!requirements.lock
!README.md
!brain/
!brain/**
!apps/
!apps/**
# The web UI (Next.js) is deployed separately. Its sources stay in the
# context because the release digest (scripts/write_source_manifest.py) covers
# all of apps/; only build output and dependencies are dropped, which the
# manifest ignores too.
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
!rules/
!rules/**
!eval/
!eval/**
!tests/
!tests/**
!scripts/
!scripts/write_source_manifest.py
!scripts/validate_lfm_release_gate.py
!deploy/
!deploy/docker-compose.prod.yml
!deploy/server_up.sh
**/__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/**
**/*.py[cod]

# Final deny rules apply after every source inclusion, at every depth.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.template
**/.npmrc
**/.pypirc
**/.brain
**/.brain/**
**/.venv
**/.venv/**
**/.vercel
**/.vercel/**
**/.git
**/.git/**
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/context_packs
**/context_packs/**
/logs/
/logs/**

**/.deploy.env
**/.deploy.env.*
**/.netrc
